- For example in browser we are opening Linkdedn and then if in the same browser, in new tab , if we open Linkdedn
then browser will open Linkdedn with the same user name. If we want to open Linkdedn of 4 different user in the same browser then we can not do it.
- Because Browser maintain the same sessions.
- This is a limitation and special feature provided by browser.
- But if we want to login with multiple user then we have two choices
	1. Do login in incognito tab
	2. Do login using another browser / browsers
- We want to use single browser with multiple user, without exchanging/sharing the sesions 
- So in Playwright we can do multirole testing 
