* how exactly playwright works or what is the phylosophy of playwright?
- Playwright guys says hey, there is a button on the page and i really want to click on that particular button 
- So how exactly playwright will work in above case 
- Playwright will check that button is not only visible on the page but it is stable also
- First we will see that element is available on the page / visible on the page 
- After that it will check that height and width is also properlly visible 
- Then it is checking that, is it really enable or not so that i can click on it?
- Then it will check that it is not getting overlapped by some other element
- Then there are some other external checks it will do like below
- is it getting blocked by some animation? or is there animation on the page or on button/on specific locator?
- It will check that, those animation are very stable or not?
- Once all above checks are done then only, playwright will say that "Button/specific" element is ready for the click
- Then playwright will click on it.
- So this is how playwright will check for the each and every element
- This is how playwright automaticaly checks internally 
- In selenium what happens that if there is any dealy for the given element then selenium will throw an error immedeately[like timeOut exception/element not found/no such element exception/stale element exception]
- Here everything is checked by playwright internally and will wait for the element to be displayed,to be stable & to be enabled then after that playwright will start intracting with the element.
- Those n number of steps which we write in other tools to interact with the element , those steps will be eleminated in the playwright
- Most of the time it will do autoscrolling as well
- Also for scrolling they have given the features
- If scroling is not working then you can write single command for the scrolling 
- No need to write complex classes 
- Playwright internally checks many things dosen't mean its very slow. It is very fast because of the architecture of the playwright
- Playwright is webSocket protocol and webSocket is superfast.
- webSocket is super fast compare to https bases protocol
- selenium is http protocol

